{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information for the reason includes the probabilities and the maximum outcomes of both lotteries. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 3000 Euros with a 25% probability, while Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 4000 Euros with a 20% probability. The difference in probabilities is 5 percentage points (25% vs. 20%), which the reason considers negligible. Therefore, the reason would focus on the maximum outcomes and prefer the lottery with the higher maximum outcome, which is Lottery B (4000 Euros).",
